IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-2-definitions`
IMPORT `chapter-2-explanations`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`

§ `Chapter 17 -- Theft, dishonest misappropriation and criminal breach of trust`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 378, 403, 405.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.

§§ `Section 378 -- Theft`

-- Whoever, intending to take dishonestly any movable property out of the
-- possession of any person without that person's consent, moves that property
-- in order to such taking, is said to commit theft.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 378"
@export Decide whether the property taking constitutes theft under Penal Code 1871 section 378
GIVEN t IS A `Property Taking` @desc The taking facts: the property (decided movable or not under s 22 from its property facts), intention to take out of possession without consent, and a moving in order to such taking.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. Theft requires that the taking be dishonest under s 24.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes theft` IF
        `the act is done dishonestly` f
    AND `is movable property within section 22` (t's `property facts`)
    AND t's `intends to take the property out of the possession of any person`
    AND t's `without that person consent`
    AND t's `moves the property in order to such taking`

§§ `Section 403 -- Dishonest misappropriation of property`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 403"
@export Decide whether the property taking constitutes dishonest misappropriation under Penal Code 1871 section 403
GIVEN t IS A `Property Taking` @desc Set dishonestly misappropriates or converts movable property to own use.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. The misappropriation must be dishonest under s 24.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes dishonest misappropriation` IF
        `the act is done dishonestly` f
    AND `is movable property within section 22` (t's `property facts`)
    AND t's `dishonestly misappropriates or converts movable property to own use`

§§ `Section 405 -- Criminal breach of trust`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 405"
@export Decide whether the trust facts constitute criminal breach of trust under Penal Code 1871 section 405
GIVEN tr IS A Trust @desc Entrustment or dominion over property, plus dishonest misappropriation or conversion, dishonest use or disposal in violation of a direction of law or legal contract, or intentionally suffering another to do so.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements for the dishonest limbs of s 405.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes criminal breach of trust` IF
        tr's `is entrusted with property or with any dominion over property`
    AND (   (    `the act is done dishonestly` f
             AND (   tr's `dishonestly misappropriates or converts that property to own use`
                  OR tr's `dishonestly uses or disposes of that property in violation of a direction of law or legal contract touching the trust`))
         OR tr's `intentionally suffers any other person to do so`)

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes theft` IF
        `constitutes theft` (a's `property taking`) (a's `fault`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes dishonest misappropriation` IF
        `constitutes dishonest misappropriation` (a's `property taking`) (a's `fault`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes criminal breach of trust` IF
        `constitutes criminal breach of trust` (a's `trust`) (a's `fault`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

§§ `Illustrations`

`dishonest taking` MEANS `Property Taking` WITH
    `property facts` IS `ordinary movable goods`
    `intends to take the property out of the possession of any person` IS TRUE
    `without that person consent` IS TRUE
    `moves the property in order to such taking` IS TRUE
    `dishonestly misappropriates or converts movable property to own use` IS FALSE
    `the theft is committed in a building tent or vessel used as a human dwelling or for the custody of property` IS FALSE
    `the accused is a clerk or servant or employed in the capacity of a clerk or servant and the property is in the possession of his master or employer` IS FALSE
    `having made preparation for causing death hurt or restraint or fear of death hurt or restraint to any person in order to commit the theft or to effect escape after it or to retain property taken by it` IS FALSE
    `knows that the property was in the possession of a deceased person at the time of that person decease and has not since been in the possession of any person legally entitled to it` IS FALSE

-- s 22 wired in: the same taking of land is not theft, because land is immovable.
`dishonest taking of land` MEANS `Property Taking` WITH
    `property facts` IS `a plot of land`
    `intends to take the property out of the possession of any person` IS TRUE
    `without that person consent` IS TRUE
    `moves the property in order to such taking` IS TRUE
    `dishonestly misappropriates or converts movable property to own use` IS FALSE
    `the theft is committed in a building tent or vessel used as a human dwelling or for the custody of property` IS FALSE
    `the accused is a clerk or servant or employed in the capacity of a clerk or servant and the property is in the possession of his master or employer` IS FALSE
    `having made preparation for causing death hurt or restraint or fear of death hurt or restraint to any person in order to commit the theft or to effect escape after it or to retain property taken by it` IS FALSE
    `knows that the property was in the possession of a deceased person at the time of that person decease and has not since been in the possession of any person legally entitled to it` IS FALSE

-- and a taking of virtual currency is: s 22 makes it property, and it is not immovable.
`dishonest taking of bitcoin` MEANS `Property Taking` WITH
    `property facts` IS `a bitcoin holding`
    `intends to take the property out of the possession of any person` IS TRUE
    `without that person consent` IS TRUE
    `moves the property in order to such taking` IS TRUE
    `dishonestly misappropriates or converts movable property to own use` IS FALSE
    `the theft is committed in a building tent or vessel used as a human dwelling or for the custody of property` IS FALSE
    `the accused is a clerk or servant or employed in the capacity of a clerk or servant and the property is in the possession of his master or employer` IS FALSE
    `having made preparation for causing death hurt or restraint or fear of death hurt or restraint to any person in order to commit the theft or to effect escape after it or to retain property taken by it` IS FALSE
    `knows that the property was in the possession of a deceased person at the time of that person decease and has not since been in the possession of any person legally entitled to it` IS FALSE

-- the s 380 circumstance: the same taking, committed inside a dwelling house.
-- s 380 itself lives in Chapter 17 -- extortion and robbery; here the circumstance
-- is carried on the taking facts, and the s 378 offence stands on its own.
`dishonest taking in a dwelling house` MEANS `Property Taking` WITH
    `property facts` IS `ordinary movable goods`
    `intends to take the property out of the possession of any person` IS TRUE
    `without that person consent` IS TRUE
    `moves the property in order to such taking` IS TRUE
    `dishonestly misappropriates or converts movable property to own use` IS FALSE
    `the theft is committed in a building tent or vessel used as a human dwelling or for the custody of property` IS TRUE
    `the accused is a clerk or servant or employed in the capacity of a clerk or servant and the property is in the possession of his master or employer` IS FALSE
    `having made preparation for causing death hurt or restraint or fear of death hurt or restraint to any person in order to commit the theft or to effect escape after it or to retain property taken by it` IS FALSE
    `knows that the property was in the possession of a deceased person at the time of that person decease and has not since been in the possession of any person legally entitled to it` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `constitutes theft` `dishonest taking` `s24 gain`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes theft` `dishonest taking of land` `s24 gain`)
#ASSERT `constitutes theft` `dishonest taking of bitcoin` `s24 gain`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes theft` `dishonest taking` `s25 slight`)

-- The s 380 circumstance reduces to TRUE on these facts, and the s 378 offence
-- it aggravates is made out on them too.
#EVAL `dishonest taking in a dwelling house`'s `the theft is committed in a building tent or vessel used as a human dwelling or for the custody of property`
#EVAL `constitutes theft` `dishonest taking in a dwelling house` `s24 gain`

